cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "frozenaudit: a protocol for auditing a released predictor under distribution shift"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying
  paper. The reference panel shipped with the ABCB1 instance has its own
  sources, which must be cited independently -- see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
type: software
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/tommyverygood/frozenaudit"
abstract: >-
  An endpoint-agnostic protocol for auditing a released predictor under
  distribution shift: freeze the decision rules and hash them, stratify a
  query set by structure-only distance to a reference set, contrast a
  candidate abstention rule against the audited model's own confidence at
  matched coverage, and evaluate pre-declared gates that can return
  not_evaluable. Ships one worked instance covering ABCB1/P-glycoprotein
  efflux risk. This is not a property predictor; the model bundles it
  redistributes are objects of evaluation in the accompanying paper and
  declare themselves development artefacts.
keywords:
  - model audit
  - applicability domain
  - selective prediction
  - abstention
  - distribution shift
  - pre-registration
  - coverage-matched evaluation
  - ABCB1
  - P-glycoprotein
# ANONYMISED FOR PEER REVIEW.
#
# The manuscript is under double-blind review and names this tool in its
# title, so a reviewer can find this repository by searching for it. The
# author block that belongs here -- four names, three affiliations and the
# two corresponding addresses -- is held out of the public repository until
# the paper is accepted, and is restored (with the missing ORCIDs for Liu
# and Li) in the same commit that adds the release DOI.
authors:
  - name: "Anonymised for peer review"
